{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler/stitch pipeline task (Task ID 5533) to create `cmd/stat/main.go` as a **contract** (skeleton/stub) file for the `stat` utility based on `srd082-stat.yaml`. The task requires:\n   - Creating `cmd/stat/main.go` with package main\n   - Declaring flag variables for all flags defined in srd082 (--format/-c, --printf, --terse/-t, --file-system/-f, --dereference/-L, --help, --version)\n   - Defining main() that calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, parses flags, iterates over file arguments\n   - Defining internal stub functions for each output mode (default format, custom format string, terse format, filesystem format)\n   - Defining internal stub functions for format directive expansion (file directives, filesystem directives)\n   - All stubs return empty strings or zero values\n   - The file must compile with `go build` and pass `go vet`\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Cobbler/stitch code generation pipeline - this is a \"contract\" task (skeleton only, not full implementation)\n   - GNU stat reimplementation in Go, verified via differential testing against `gstat` (Homebrew)\n   - pkg/sys.Stat and pkg/sys.Lstat for file metadata (FileInfo struct)\n   - pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() for SIGPIPE handling\n   - Go `flag` package for flag parsing (standard library, not cobra for cmd/ utilities)\n   - Format directive expansion (printf-style `%a`, `%A`, `%b`, etc.)\n   - Separate file vs filesystem mode with different format directives\n   - SPDX copyright header required on every Go file\n   - E8: 40-line function limit; E9: 500-line file limit\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd082-stat.yaml` (READ)\n     - Source of truth for all