ncountered yet as implementation hasn't started\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full task prompt with extensive project context, SRD references, execution constitution, coding standards, constraints, task description (create cmd/stat/main.go contract), requirements R1-R4, design decisions D1-D2, and acceptance criteria AC1-AC4.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Instruction to provide a summary instead of continuing implementation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/stat/main.go` with all required flag declarations, main() function, and stub functions\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/stat ./cmd/stat/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/stat/...`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two source files needed for implementation:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd082-stat.yaml` - to understand all flags and requirement groups\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` - to confirm the SIGPIPE handler API\n   \n   I was about to write `cmd/stat/main.go` with the following structure:\n   - Copyright header\n   - Package main, imports (flag, fmt, os, pkg/sys)\n   - Flag variables: `formatStr`, `printfStr`, `terse`, `fileSystem`, `dereference`\n   - main() calling InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), flag.Parse(), iterating os.Args\n   - Stub functions: `defaultFormat(*sys.FileInfo, string) string`, `customFormat(*sys.FileInfo, string, string) string`, `terseFormat(*sys.FileInfo, string) string`, `filesystemFormat(string) string`, `expandFileDirective(byte, *sys.FileInfo, string) string`, `expandFilesystemDirective(byte, string) string`\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the `cmd/stat/main.go` file. The task description states: \"Create cmd/stat/main.go with package main. Declare flag variables for all flags defined in srd082-stat.yaml\" and \"Define main() that calls sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), parses flags via flag.Parse(), iterates over remaining arguments as file paths, and calls placeholder stub